post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Aether is installed under /etc/xdg/quickshell/aether. It can coexist with
caelestia-shell-git; only one of the two shells should be running.

Nothing else is needed to build or start it.

Start the shell now:
    aether shell -d

After an upgrade, restart the running copy:
    aether shell -r -d

See what is running and how to talk to it:
    aether shell -l
    aether shell -s        # list every IPC target and function

Hyprland starts the shell, so add this to your config once:

    Lua config (~/.config/hypr/hyprland/execs.lua):
        hl.exec_cmd("aether shell -d")

    hyprlang config (~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf):
        exec-once = aether shell -d

Keybinds are not installed into ~/.config/hypr -- that file is yours. The
complete reference config, including every keybind and variable the settings
pages write, is at:

    /usr/share/aether-shell/hypr/

Compare its hyprland/keybinds.lua and variables.lua with your own setup. Do not
copy the whole tree over ~/.config/hypr without reading it: it is a full config,
not a fragment. Until then, these still work from a terminal:

    aether ipc call nexus open      # open the settings window
    aether ipc call drawers toggle launcher

Optional extras:
    hyprmoncfg              saved monitor layouts (Display page)
    bluez                   Bluetooth and the pairing agent
    fprintd / howdy-next    fingerprint / face unlock
    xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland  screen sharing and file pickers

Qt application theming (optional): the Qt platform theme is installed. Add this
to ~/.config/caelestia/hypr-user.lua and log back in:

    hl.env("QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME", "aether")

The shell writes only ~/.config/caelestia/. It never edits ~/.config/hypr.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}

pre_remove() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Aether's configuration is kept in ~/.config/caelestia/ and is not removed by
this package. Delete it yourself if you also want to drop your settings.
EOF
}
